.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-PLAN\-JOB\-RESCORE" "1" "" "roark-simulation-plan-job-rescore" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-plan\-job\-rescore \- Re\-score a simulation run
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation plan job rescore
\fIjob\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Grade a finished run's calls again, without placing new calls: the same calls, graded on the run plan's metrics as they are now. Metrics on the plan grade every call of the run, metrics attached to a flow grade that flow's calls, each at its current version, and Agent Expectations grades against the flows' current expectations. Use it after changing a plan's metrics, a metric, or a flow's expectations, to see how the run you already have scores against them. The metrics graded are listed in `metrics` and become the run's metric set: the run's results, checks and report read them from then on. The new values replace the run's current ones; earlier values stay in each metric value's history. The grading is billed like any metric collection. A run is re\-scored one at a time: while one re\-score runs, another is refused with 409. Returns immediately. Poll GET /v1/simulation/plan/job/{jobId}/rescore until `status` is COMPLETED or FAILED, then read the new values from GET /v1/simulation/plan/job/{jobId}/results.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/simulation/plan/job/{jobId}/rescore
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIjob\-id\fR
The job\-id.
